o take lessons immediately because they were very tired of driving me around everywhere.","end_ms":266977,"start_ms":259697},{"text":" Now, Neil, I know that you have recently been on a little trip, haven''t you?","end_ms":273037,"start_ms":266977},{"text":" You went to the Lake District in the north of England.","end_ms":275857,"start_ms":273037},{"text":" I did, and it''s fantastically beautiful.","end_ms":281097,"start_ms":275857},{"text":" There are mountains and lakes, and it''s very lush green because of all the rain.","end_ms":288837,"start_ms":281097},{"text":" And you can go hiking, and you can see fantastic scenery.","end_ms":295317,"start_ms":288837},{"text":" It''s a great place.","end_ms":296317,"start_ms":295317},{"text":" Would you say it''s your favourite countryside area in the UK?","end_ms":300717,"start_ms":296317},{"text":" Yeah, probably. I mean, parts of Scotland are really spectacular, with even bigger mountains.","end_ms":309197,"start_ms":301677},{"text":" But in England, the Lake District is fantastic. And in Wales, I recently went to the Pembrokeshire","end_ms":317037,"start_ms":309917},{"text":" coast that in the west of Wales and there just stunning scenery there beaches coastal walks fantastic Yes I saw the photos of that trip It looked amazing My favourite countryside area is probably Cornwall and Devon the southwest of England","end_ms":336965,"start_ms":317037},{"text":" Once you start driving down there, the roads are very small. There''s not a lot of busy traffic.","end_ms":345685,"start_ms":338245},{"text":" It can be quite stressful though because the roads are one way and on either side of the","end_ms":353025,"start_ms":345685},{"text":" road you have these big hedges so you can''t really see around the corners and if a car","end_ms":358685,"start_ms":353025},{"text":" is coming towards you it''s not good.","end_ms":361625,"start_ms":358685},{"text":" No, it''s a nightmare.","end_ms":363165,"start_ms":361625},{"text":" You might have to reverse for ages.","end_ms":365365,"start_ms":363165},{"text":" Yeah.","end_ms":366365,"start_ms":365365},{"text":" I really hate that.","end_ms":373625,"start_ms":366365},{"text":" now then to recap the vocabulary that we''ve used in this episode, starting with countryside.","end_ms":379625,"start_ms":373625},{"text":" Now, the countryside is the area outside of the cities where not many people live and there''s","end_ms":387065,"start_ms":379625},{"text":" lots of nature and wildlife. Yes, and wildlife is animals which live in natural environments,","end_ms":394105,"start_ms":387065},{"text":" for example, badgers and birds. We''ve also heard the adjective","end_ms":398265,"start_ms":394105},{"text":" lush which describes a green area full of","end_ms":401785,"start_ms":398265},{"text":" healthy plants and trees.","end_ms":403545,"start_ms":401785},{"text":" We also heard the adjective remote which","end_ms":405865,"start_ms":403545},{"text":" describes a place that''s far away from","end_ms":408265,"start_ms":405865},{"text":" towns and cities.","end_ms":409865,"start_ms":408265},{"text":" We also heard scenery and scenery is what","end_ms":412825,"start_ms":409865},{"text":" you can see in a place and in the","end_ms":414905,"start_ms":412825},{"text":" countryside the scenery is often beautiful.","end_ms":417705,"start_ms":414905},{"text":" OK, well that is it for this episode of","end_ms":420025,"start_ms":417705},{"text":" Real Easy English but don''t forget to sign","end_ms":422665,"start_ms":420025},{"text":" up to our email newsletter. You can get","end_ms":424985,"start_ms":422665},{"text":" weekly tips and updates from your favourite","end_ms":427305,"start_ms":424985},{"text":" presenters. We''ll be back next week with another episode, but bye for now. Goodbye.","end_ms":431785,"start_ms":427305}],"timestamps":[{"word":"Hi","index":0,"end_ms":340,"start_ms":160},{"word":"Georgie,","index":1,"end_ms":780,"start_ms":340},{"word":"how","index":2,